! Detailed n-Heptane mechanism 
! Supplement to the publication
!------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Comprehensive kinetic modeling and experimental study of a fuel-rich, premixed n heptane flame
! L. Seidel, K. Moshammer, X. Wang, T. Zeuch, K. Kohse-Höinghaus, F. Mauss
!------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
! n-Heptane: N-C7H16
!-------------------
! List of major updates
! + The C1-C4 chemistry is based on the mechanism of
!   -Schenk et al. Combust. Flame (2013) 487-503 which is based on
!   -Oßwald et al. Z. Phys Chem. 225 (2011) 1029-1054 which is based on
!   -Hoyermann et al. Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys. (6) (2004) 3824-3835
! + This mechanism also includes an updated Ethanol, Benzene and Toluene chemistry compiled
!   from various sources
! + The PAH formation chemistry is based on the PhD thesis from Fabian Mauss 
!   with modification discussed in the publication
! + The n-Heptane reaction scheme is based on the detailed scheme published in
!   Ahmed et al. Z.Phys. Chem. 223 (2009) 551-563 with the following modifications:
!   - more possible products are considered due to extended C1-C4 chemistry
!   - Species have been renamed
!   - Updated rates for H abstraction and beta scission of C7H15 and C7H14
!     isomers
!   - Low temperature chemistry for butene and butane isomers
!------------------
